  "answer_markdown": "I conditionally recommend **Firecrawl for a first validation** of search and web scanning: the supplied README read dated 2026-10-11 describes search with full result content and extraction into Markdown/JSON; the primary language in the catalog snapshot is TypeScript. The inferred benefit for a RAG product is preparing web materials for further processing, but quality on the target pages has not been checked. In the recommendation list, Firecrawl is counted once by its canonical identity: secondary categories and the former name `mendableai/firecrawl` do not create separate tools. This removes catalog duplicates; deduplication of collected content remains a separate task. The candidate order expresses the host's preference, while suitability and compatibility of both selected repositories remain unverified. [Firecrawl README](https://github.com/firecrawl/firecrawl).\n\nProposed data flow: query or public URL → Firecrawl → Markdown/JSON → application-owned validation, normalization and deduplication → the downstream RAG pipeline, whose structure is currently unknown. **Firecrawl MCP Server** is conditionally needed if the client uses MCP: it is a separate TypeScript adapter to the service, rather than a second crawler; without such a client, adding it is not justified. According to the supplied README dated 2026-10-11, hosted mode allows rate-limited keyless scrape/search/parse, while crawl/map/agent require a key; local cloud mode also requires a key, and the self-hosted API URL is configurable. These options have not been activated. The team retains responsibility for the boundary at which queries are sent to an external service, content provenance, queues, retries and storage integration. [Firecrawl MCP Server README](https://github.com/firecrawl/firecrawl-mcp-server).\n\nComplexity is determined by workload, the application's language and platform, the chosen version, extraction quality, dependencies, limits and maintenance. The supplied README indicates primarily AGPL-3.0 for the core and MIT for SDKs and some UI components; the adapter's MIT license in the snapshot does not replace checking the core's license. Cloud has additional capabilities, and self-hosting equivalence has not been established: an unacceptable license or the absence of a required feature in an allowed mode would reverse the preference for Firecrawl. At equivalent scope—search, content retrieval, Markdown/JSON, error handling and integration—a custom implementation requires developing and maintaining these parts; the existing/native path should be compared against the same criteria, but it is unknown, so savings have not been demonstrated. The catalog records observations from 2026-09-01; separate host reads dated 2026-10-11 refine the assessment without updating the catalog or eligibility. The pack is limited: 12 cards were retained from 18 candidates, with coverage of NanmiCoder/MediaCrawler, zcaceres/fetch-mcp, runesleo/x-reader, browser-use/browser-use, ArchiveBox/ArchiveBox and kimtaeyoon83/mcp-server-youtube-transcript lost because of the budget. Their omission and unknown or truncated fields do not prove capability absence; the comparison is incomplete.\n\nFor scenario `CP04-HOLD-12-first-validation`, only a **hypothetical first-validation budget of 4–8 engineer-hours** is specified, with low confidence: one engineer familiar with the target application and its component interface, at 8 hours per engineer-day and an allocated capacity of one engineer. Before any integration, the workload, existing path, language/platform, version and license must be confirmed. Source qualification or an isolated synthetic fixture is proposed: use the chosen version's documentation to check the search and Markdown/JSON contract, mode limitations and handling of repeated URLs and content against predefined examples; this will not prove live quality. The validation boundary excludes network access, installation, credentials, a paid provider and production data. All steps have the status `proposed_not_executed`; full adoption effort and elapsed working days remain unknown. Since the existing path is not described, the trial must remain isolated, without changing authoritative data or queues; abandoning it preserves current processing. Actual integration requires a separate explicit request.",
